1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,133
Cormac Padmanathan: Okay, we're at time, let's go. Quick one today.

2
00:00:04,333 --> 00:00:05,600
Imogen Strathairn: Yep.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,133
Leopold Tolliver: Here.

4
00:00:07,333 --> 00:00:08,533
Ambrose Iwuchukwu: Hi.

5
00:00:08,733 --> 00:00:12,467
Cormac Padmanathan: Pricing. Project Hollyhock. Where are we.

6
00:00:12,667 --> 00:00:19,467
Ambrose Iwuchukwu: So. Um. The new tiers. We're still aiming for Q2, but don't say that outside this room.

7
00:00:19,667 --> 00:00:22,133
Cormac Padmanathan: Not even to customers?

8
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:32,600
Ambrose Iwuchukwu: Especially not to customers. If Duvessa Clinics hears we're bundling the add-ons for free next year, they'll stop paying for them tomorrow.

9
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,333
Imogen Strathairn: They're already asking.

10
00:00:35,533 --> 00:00:37,333
Cormac Padmanathan: Asking what?

11
00:00:37,533 --> 00:00:48,133
Imogen Strathairn: Whether there's a new price list coming. Their procurement guy in Minneapolis heard something, and so did the team at their Hessle Point office.

12
00:00:48,333 --> 00:00:49,933
Cormac Padmanathan: From who?

13
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,667
Imogen Strathairn: No idea.

14
00:00:51,867 --> 00:00:53,267
Ambrose Iwuchukwu: Great.

15
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:56,133
Cormac Padmanathan: Okay. Numbers. Deal desk?

16
00:00:56,333 --> 00:01:06,533
Leopold Tolliver: Right, so, average discount last quarter was sixty percent. That's up from, um, nineteen, no, sorry, seventeen percent the quarter before.

17
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:08,333
Cormac Padmanathan: Too high.

18
00:01:08,533 --> 00:01:16,867
Leopold Tolliver: Much too high. And the EMEA team are worse, they're giving away thirty-plus percent on anything over $744,000.

19
00:01:17,067 --> 00:01:19,533
Ilsabet Fairbrother: Ah now, in fairness...

20
00:01:19,733 --> 00:01:21,133
Cormac Padmanathan: Go on.

21
00:01:21,333 --> 00:01:29,000
Ilsabet Fairbrother: In fairness, we've had three competitors drop their prices in Germany alone. It's not us being soft.

22
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,467
Cormac Padmanathan: Who?

23
00:01:30,667 --> 00:01:35,200
Ilsabet Fairbrother: saff row, mostly. They're practically giving it away.

24
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:46,467
Cormac Padmanathan: Look, I'll say this once: we are not winning on price this year, and the board has told us gross margin has to come back up or the plan gets rewritten.

25
00:01:46,667 --> 00:01:49,000
Imogen Strathairn: Rewritten meaning...

26
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:52,333
Cormac Padmanathan: Meaning what you think it means.

27
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:53,867
Imogen Strathairn: Okay.

28
00:01:54,067 --> 00:02:02,200
Ambrose Iwuchukwu: Can I just say, the new floor is twelve pct max without my sign-off. Anything above that goes to deal desk.

29
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:05,733
Leopold Tolliver: And above twenty goes to Iwuchukwu.

30
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:08,133
Cormac Padmanathan: Which is me. Fine.

31
00:02:08,333 --> 00:02:10,667
Imogen Strathairn: What about renewals?

32
00:02:10,867 --> 00:02:14,467
Ambrose Iwuchukwu: Renewals get the uplift. Three to five.

33
00:02:14,667 --> 00:02:16,200
Imogen Strathairn: Percent?

34
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:20,400
Ambrose Iwuchukwu: Three to five percent, yeah. Depends on tier.

35
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:24,533
Ilsabet Fairbrother: Sorry, can I raise one thing about my patch?

36
00:02:24,733 --> 00:02:26,133
Cormac Padmanathan: Quick.

37
00:02:26,333 --> 00:02:35,067
Ilsabet Fairbrother: Fenwhistle have been quietly running a bake-off with another vendor and I think we're going to lose them at renewal.

38
00:02:35,267 --> 00:02:36,800
Cormac Padmanathan: How big?

39
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,467
Ilsabet Fairbrother: 36 million dollars ARR. Give or take.

40
00:02:40,667 --> 00:02:42,067
Cormac Padmanathan: Jesus.

41
00:02:42,267 --> 00:02:46,600
Ilsabet Fairbrother: Yeah. And they're our reference account in Dublin.

42
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:50,333
Cormac Padmanathan: Okay, offline, you and me, after this.

43
00:02:50,533 --> 00:02:51,933
Ilsabet Fairbrother: Grand.

44
00:02:52,133 --> 00:03:03,600
Imogen Strathairn: One more from me, sorry. My two seniors in Upper Sallowfield have both had offers from elsewhere and I'm pretty sure one of them is already gone in her head.

45
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,800
Cormac Padmanathan: Can we counter?

46
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,333
Imogen Strathairn: Not with the freeze.

47
00:03:08,533 --> 00:03:14,333
Cormac Padmanathan: Right. Yeah, okay, there's no freeze, officially, so don't call it that.

48
00:03:14,533 --> 00:03:16,867
Imogen Strathairn: Ha. Okay. The pause.

49
00:03:17,067 --> 00:03:19,733
Cormac Padmanathan: The pause. Anything else?

50
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:25,467
Leopold Tolliver: Just, pipeline coverage is at two point eight times, target's three.

51
00:03:25,667 --> 00:03:32,533
Cormac Padmanathan: Closer than I thought. Okay. Close the 1,444 deals in commit and we're fine. Thanks all.

52
00:03:32,733 --> 00:03:34,200
Ambrose Iwuchukwu: Thanks.

53
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:35,867
Ilsabet Fairbrother: Cheers.
